# why: every feature adds rows to the ADR index; two features merging add different rows, and
# a union merge keeps both instead of stopping the stack sync on an add/add conflict. The
# src/adr-index.repo.test.ts check keeps the table complete and in order.
docs/internal/adr/README.md merge=union

# why: a Windows checkout would otherwise turn text files into CRLF, which breaks the tests that
# compare file text and the scripts bash runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# why: the Windows process-table fixture is a captured PowerShell answer; its CRLF line ends are part of what the parser reads.
src/ports/fixtures/win32-process-table.txt -text
